# `golem/inspector`

**Agent (`golem/inspector`):** `Attach(ctx, srv, schema, opts)` dials the hub's `/ws/agent` with a bearer token, registers the generated `InspectorSchema()`, and stays idle until the hub sends `ObserveStart`. It reads entities only inside `Server.ObserveReplication` callbacks on the tick goroutine: a snapshot from `All()`/`FullUpdate()`, then per-entity dirty masks accumulated from `LastFlushMask()` and encoded with `MarshalDeltaMask` at most `RateHz` per second. Snapshots and batches are queued as single items; a full queue drops the stream and restarts it with a new epoch. It never blocks the tick loop, never filters by interest, visibility or ownership, and is disabled when `HubURL` is empty.

**Wire (`golem/inspector/wire`):** hand-written codec for `inspector.proto` on top of `golem/pb.Writer` with a bounds-checked reader (decoders return errors, never panic). Owns the `Schema` descriptor and `EntityFields`, the game-agnostic merge of generated State/Delta messages (a set mask bit whose field is absent resets it). `testdata/` golden fixtures are shared with the TypeScript codec in `golem-inspector/`; regenerate with `go test ./golem/inspector/wire -update` and rerun `npm test` there after any protocol change.

**Hub (`golem/inspector/hub`):** target registry, per-target world store, cold-observation refcount with grace stop, per-browser bounded queues with resync/slow-consumer handling, shared-password sessions, JSON REST, metrics and static UI hosting. All state is under one mutex; sockets are written only by their own writer goroutines.

**Boundaries:** `wire` and `hub` must not import `golem` (the hub binary stays free of the runtime). Only the agent imports `golem`. Runtime hooks the agent needs belong in `golem/replication_observer.go`, not in agent-specific code inside the tick loop. The inspector is read-only and entity-only.
